Let me check the scheduler trigger result file and also check if the backend is still processing. The file /tmp/sched_investor.json doesn't exist yet, which means the HTTP request is still in progress (180s timeout) or the curl process was killed. Let me check if the curl process is still running.

Actually, looking more carefully — the investor engine's previous run took 603,596ms = ~10 minutes. I triggered it at 19:40Z. It's now ~19:52Z, which is 12 minutes. The run should be close to completing or already completed. But I'm not seeing a new record.

Wait — the issue might be that the `inFlight` set was not cleared. Looking at the code:
```
try {
    ...run engine...
    return result;
} finally {
    inFlight.delete(kind);
}
```

The `inFlight` set should be cleared in the `finally` block. But if the previous run crashed (e.g., process restart), the `inFlight` set would be reset since it's in-memory.

Actually, the backend was restarted at 19:39Z (bootTime: 2026-07-26T19:39:10.049Z), so the `inFlight` set would be empty. The new trigger at 19:40Z should have started the job.

Let me check if the HTTP request is still running or if it timed out. The curl had `--max-time 180`, so it would have timed out at 19:43Z (3 minutes after 19:40Z). But the file doesn't exist yet... Actually, `nohup` might have issues with the output redirection.

Let me just keep polling. The backend should complete the run regardless of the HTTP timeout. Let me wait a few more minutes and check again.

Actually, I notice the investor engine takes a very long time (10+ minutes) because it queries SEC EDGAR 12 times with different queries. The Free tier on Render may have limited resources. Let me wait longer and poll.

But actually, I should also consider: maybe the scheduler API endpoint itself has a timeout. The Render Free tier has a 100-second request timeout. If the request takes longer than 100s, Render kills the HTTP connection but the backend process continues. So the curl would get an error, but the backend would continue processing.

